.\" nulldc3-joyconfig.1:

.TH  "NULLDC3-JOYCONFIG" "1" "August 27, 2015" "NULLDC3-JOYCONFIG" "nulldc3-joyconfig"

.SH NAME

nulldc3-joyconfig \- An editor for nullDC controller mappings.

.SH SYNOPSIS

\fBnulldc3-joyconfig\fR [-h | [-d DEVICE_ID] [-f FILE]]

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

\fBnulldc3-joyconfig\fR assists you when creating custom mappings for \fBnulldc3\fR, the nullDC Dreamcast emulator.
It reads them from mappings/ in its directory: the directory of its executable, the one of \fB--portable\fR \fIdir\fR,
or with \fB--shared\fR ~/.config/nulldc3 ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nulldc3).

.SH "EXAMPLE COMMANDLINE"

.TP
\fBNo command line options will give you a list of devices that you can choose from and then start the mapping assistant.\fR
nulldc3-joyconfig

.TP
\fBCreate a mapping for /dev/input/event3.\fR
nulldc3-joyconfig -d 3

.TP
\fBCreate a mapping for /dev/input/event3 and save the mapping file to mappings/my_mapping.cfg of a nulldc3 whose executable is in ~/nulldc3.\fR
nulldc3-joyconfig -d 3 -f ~/nulldc3/mappings/my_mapping.cfg

.TP
\fBThe same for a nulldc3 that is run with --shared.\fR
nulldc3-joyconfig -d 3 -f ~/.config/nulldc3/mappings/my_mapping.cfg

.SH "GENERAL OPTIONS"

.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
Show a short help text.

.TP
\fB-d DEVICE_ID\fR, \fB--device-id DEVICE_ID\fR
Create a mapping for a specific device. The device ID is the number X from /dev/input/eventX.

\fB-f FILE\fR, \fB--file FILE\fR
Save the created mapping to a file. By default, the mapping will be printed to the standard output.

.SH "KNOWN ISSUES"

If you're using a wireless controller, please make sure it is on before creating a mapping. Some controllers emit "Button Pressed/Released" signals when turning them on, which may lead to wrongly mapped keys.

.SH "PYTHON VERSION"

.TP
\fBnulldc3-joyconfig\fR is written in Python and needs the evdev module to work:
\fIhttps://pypi.python.org/pypi/evdev\fP

.TP
Distributions like Ubuntu have the evdev module as a package in their repositories - in these cases you should use your package manager instead of pip to install it.

.TP
Although \fBnulldc3-joyconfig\fR does support both Python 2.6 or higher and 3.0 or higher, you need to run \fBnulldc3-joyconfig\fR with the same Python version that you installed the evdev module for, i.e. if you installed the evdev module for Python 2, you also need to run \fBnulldc3-joyconfig\fR using Python 2 and vice-versa.

